🎓 Campus Portal — Student Notes Management System

A responsive, front-end-only web app for browsing, searching, and sharing student notes/past papers. Built with plain **HTML, CSS, and JavaScript** — no frameworks, no backend, no build step.

---

## ✨ Features

- **Login page** with a centered card, gradient background, and email/password fields
- **Dashboard** with quick stats, a welcome banner, an auto-rotating image slider, and quick-action shortcuts
- **Notes page** with a searchable grid of subject cards (Physics, Maths, Chemistry, etc.)
- **Upload page** with a validated form for adding new notes
- Fully **responsive layout** (sidebar collapses to a top bar on tablets/phones)
- Shared **Poppins** typography and a consistent blue color system via CSS variables

### JavaScript functionality (`script.js`)

| # | Feature | Where it lives |
|---|---------|-----------------|
| 1 | **Dynamic Content Updates** — live filtering of the notes grid as you type, with a "no results" state | `pastpapers.html` |
| 2 | **Interactive Image Slider** — auto-rotating + manual prev/next/dot navigation, pauses on hover | `dashboard.html` |
| 3 | **Form Validation** — real-time email/password checks on login, and subject/year/PDF checks on upload | `index.html`, `upload.html` |
| 4 | **Custom Animations** — staggered fade/slide-in on page load, scroll-triggered reveals, button pulse feedback, shake animation on invalid fields | All pages |

All animations and slider/validation styles are injected by `script.js` itself, so `style.css` doesn't need to be touched to make them work.

---


---


## 🛠️ Tech Stack

- **HTML5** — semantic page structure
- **CSS3** — custom properties (CSS variables), Flexbox, Grid, media queries
- **Vanilla JavaScript (ES6)** — no libraries or frameworks
- **Google Fonts** — [Poppins](https://fonts.google.com/specimen/Poppins)

---

